smb: client: Clear sensitive stack data in cifsencrypt.c

jira KERNEL-1962
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.27.1.el9_9
commit-author Thomas Huth <thuth@redhat.com>
commit 1a6bd74a27f1007b02c5a30aaa35608286bd0d23
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.27.1.el9_9/1a6bd74a.failed

Make sure to not leak hash data via the stack, clear it
with memzero_explicit() before leaving the function.

	Signed-off-by: Thomas Huth <thuth@redhat.com>
	Signed-off-by: Namjae Jeon <linkinjeon@kernel.org>
	Signed-off-by: Paulo Alcantara <pc@manguebit.org>
(cherry picked from commit 1a6bd74a27f1007b02c5a30aaa35608286bd0d23)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

